# A stream cut mid-text via disconnect_after: the retry loop sees a
# provider.StreamInterrupted, humanised (internal/tui/bridge.go
# humaniseRetryError) as plain "Stream interrupted" (no status code to
# report), then reconnects and delivers the rest of the answer in full.
# The retry backoff is fixed at ten minutes, so the cut partial text and
# the countdown stay on screen until the scenario presses r (retry now).
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-disconnect-midstream.yaml
@env HARNESS_RETRY_DELAY_MS=600000

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE trigger a mid-stream disconnect
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Streaming a reply/ 20
SHOT partial-before-cut
WAITFOR /Stream interrupted[\s\S]*Retrying in \d+s · attempt 2 of 4 · r to retry now/ 20
SHOT countdown
EXPECT /Streaming a reply/
KEY r
WAITFOR /Reconnected on attempt 2/ 20
EXPECT /Reconnected on attempt 2/
SHOT reconnected
WAITFOR /Reconnected, and here is the rest of the answer in full/ 20
SHOT final-reply
EXPECT /Reconnected, and here is the rest of the answer in full/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
